    "body": "Closes #97.\n\nImplements ADR-007 in two commits: the owned DOM, then the lexbor converter that produces it.\n\n## Commit 1 — `feat(dom)`\n\nAdds `honeybee::renderer::dom::Node`, `Element`, `TextNode`, `Document`.\n- Tree owns children via `std::unique_ptr<Node>`\n- Nodes are non-copyable and non-movable, so `parent_` back-pointers never dangle\n- `Document::title()` finds the first `<title>` anywhere in the tree\n- `Node::text_content()` concatenates all descendant text\n- 9 unit tests covering children, attributes, hierarchy, deep nesting, title lookup\n\n## Commit 2 — `feat(html)`\n\nRefactors `renderer/html` from a document type into a producer.\n- `html::parse(std::string_view) -> std::unique_ptr<dom::Document>` walks lexbor's tree once, then destroys the lexbor document\n- Deletes the old RAII wrapper `html::Document` (`document.hpp/cpp`)\n- Rewrites `preview.cpp` to use `parse()` + `find_element(\"body\")` — preserving the original body-only text extraction\n- Adds `Node::find_element(tag)` — used by both `preview` and `title()`\n- 8 converter tests (including a fully-owned-lifetime test that would UB-fail if any lexbor pointer leaked)\n\n## Behavior parity\n\n`tests/test_preview.cpp` is **unchanged**. Its 15 assertions still pass, proving the refactor preserved `make_preview`'s contract.\n\n`src/browser/window.cpp` is **unchanged**. It only calls `make_preview`, which is unchanged in signature and behavior.\n\n## lexbor isolation\n\nAfter this PR, only `src/renderer/html/convert.cpp` includes lexbor headers. Per ADR-007's consequence #4.\n\n## Next\n\nPhase 2 (CSS) becomes possible: `renderer::dom` is now a stable, owned tree with no parser coupling.",
